\b Frontend Reference Document\b0\par
\pard This document summarizes the frontend part of the BRD Accelerator project, including its features, functionalities, and technology stack.\par
\pard\par
\b 1. Overview\b0\par
The frontend is the user-facing part of the BRD Accelerator application. It provides an interactive workflow for uploading business requirements documents, reviewing extracted requirements, managing user stories, validating outputs, and exporting results.\par
\pard\par
\b 2. Frontend Functionalities\b0\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Dashboard: Displays summary cards for projects, epics, stories, quality score, and coverage.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 BRD Upload: Supports drag-and-drop upload and file browsing for common document formats.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Project Management: Shows workflows/projects with search and pagination.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Requirements Review: Allows viewing, filtering, editing, and approving requirements.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Epic Generation: Groups generated stories into epics with search and pagination.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 User Stories Management: Supports table and board view for managing stories.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Story Details and Review: Displays detailed story information, acceptance criteria, and business rules.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Validation / QA: Shows validation score, issues, and recommendations.\par
\pard\li720\fi-720\bullet\tx720 Export: Supports exporting in PDF, Word, and Excel formats.\par
\pard\par
\b 3. Tech Stack Used\b0\par
Frontend Core: React, TypeScript\par
Build Tool: Vite\par
Routing: TanStack Router, TanStack Start\par
State/Data Fetching: React Query\par
Styling: Tailwind CSS\par
UI Libraries: Radix UI, shadcn-style component structure\par
Forms and Validation: React Hook Form, Zod\par
Icons and Visualization: Lucide React, Recharts\par
Utilities: clsx, tailwind-merge, date-fns\par
\pard\par
\b 4. Where These Technologies Are Used\b0\par
React and TypeScript are used across the route pages and UI components.\par
TanStack Router is used in the router setup and route definitions.\par
React Query is used for fetching workflow data in the pages.\par
Tailwind CSS is used for styling the app layout and pages.\par
Radix UI components are used in the UI component library.\par
API communication is handled in the API utility file.\par
\pard\par
\b 5. Summary\b0\par
The frontend is built as a modern, interactive workflow application that helps users move from uploaded BRD content to structured requirements, epics, user stories, validation, and export.\par
